                                    <div class="faq-section" style="margin-top:40px;">
                                        <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
                                        <h3>What's a fair monthly retainer for a digital marketing agency in Mumbai in 2026?</h3>
                                        <p>Realistic ranges: freelancer ₹15K–₹50K/month; boutique specialist ₹50K–₹1.5L/month; full-stack accountable agency ₹1L–₹3L/month; large network agency ₹3L–₹15L+/month. Below ₹50K total, you can't fund the team needed to actually move metrics. Below ₹1L, it's hard to get true full-stack accountability.</p>
                                        <h3>How is ITD GrowthLabs different from other Mumbai agencies?</h3>
                                        <p>Our flagship is Ready-to-Buy Lead Generation — AI-filtered, multi-platform, fully managed, accountable for qualified leads delivered to your Sheet in real time, not for raw click volume. Most agencies sell campaigns. We sell qualified leads. We're in the ₹1L–₹3L/month tier and openly say no to bad-fit work.</p>
                                        <h3>Should I hire a Mumbai-based agency or a remote one?</h3>
                                        <p>Geography stopped mattering for most marketing work post-2020. Mumbai-specific value: brand video / photography production, local SEO for Mumbai-physical businesses, Mumbai-based creator activations, and senior partner-led brand work. For everything else (ads, SEO, content, lead-gen, analytics), skill beats location.</p>
                                        <h3>How do I verify a Mumbai agency is legit before signing?</h3>
                                        <p>Run the 6-question vetting test: active client list (not portfolio archive), real reporting example with leads/CAC/conversion (not impressions/reach), named senior team members on your account, 12+ month average client tenure, 2 references you can call without them on the line, specific 90-day plan (not 12-month narrative). Most agencies fail at least 2 of these.</p>
                                        <h3>What's the difference between a boutique and a full-stack agency?</h3>
                                        <p>Boutique (₹50K–₹1.5L/month) goes deep on 1–2 channels — social, or ads, or SEO — with specialist execution. Full-stack (₹1L–₹3L/month) ties multiple channels into an integrated lead-gen system with account direction and outcome accountability. Boutique is right when you've already figured out which channel works; full-stack is right when you need someone to figure that out and execute it.</p>
                                        <h3>How quickly should I see results from a Mumbai digital marketing agency?</h3>
                                        <p>Paid channels (Google, Meta): first leads within 2–4 weeks, optimised performance by month 2–3. SEO: first ranking shifts in 6–12 weeks, real traffic lift by month 4–6. Content: similar to SEO. Full-stack lead-gen systems: first qualified leads in week 2–3 post-onboarding, system optimisation through weeks 4–8. Anyone promising 'leads in week 1' is selling the wrong thing.</p>
                                        <h3>Should I work with a Mumbai agency for international markets (US, UK, UAE, Australia)?</h3>
                                        <p>Yes — most full-stack Mumbai agencies (including ITD GrowthLabs) serve international clients well. The advantage: India studio cost economics, India agency talent depth, time-zone overlap with most of the world. The honest constraint: if your campaigns need US/UK cultural nuance for B2C creative, a local agency may catch idiom you'd miss. For B2B lead-gen, ads, SEO, content — geography is mostly noise.</p>
